  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The latest fiscal data from Indonesia reflects a complex economic landscape as the government balances various expenditures and revenue streams. According to official reports, Bank Indonesia achieved a budget surplus of Rp117.8 trillion as of September 2026. This fiscal outlook is accompanied by significant sector-specific financial figures. For instance, the state electricity company, PLN, has reported that electricity subsidies allocated to data centers have reached Rp8 trillion. Meanwhile, the government continues to manage substantial obligations, with health sector spending recorded at Rp664 trillion and total debt among state-owned enterprises reaching Rp1,604 trillion. Other revenue indicators include digital tax collections amounting to Rp60.1 trillion. These figures are part of broader ongoing assessments of Indonesia’s national budget performance, involving data collection from various state institutions and authorities monitoring economic trends throughout the year.",
